What I Learned:
A golden image is a standard, pre-configured template used to deploy systems consistently. It provides the same software, configuration, and security settings across multiple systems.
RHEL Image Builder is used to create customised RHEL system images instead of configuring every system manually.

Image Builder Options
•	Insights Image Builder → hosted through the Red Hat Hybrid Cloud Console.
•	RHEL Image Builder → runs locally on a RHEL system and can be managed through the command line or RHEL Web Console.
Insights Image Builder = hosted
RHEL Image Builder = local

Blueprints
A blueprint defines what should be included in the final system image. It can specify packages, users, configuration, networking, security settings, services, and other system requirements.
Blueprint = specification
Image = finished system
This connects to the Robot World project because a blueprint could define a consistent environment for deploying the Java application instead of manually configuring each server.

Image Building Process
Create blueprint → Define system requirements → Build image → Deploy image
Once a blueprint is created, it can be reused to produce consistent system images.

Overall Understanding
The main idea is standardised and repeatable deployment: define the desired system once, build an image from that definition, and reuse it across environments.

